// bites: (1) these are not settings, they are the running game; (2) the ENGINE saves the render device's config on
// exit, so a property changed in memory would end up written to the player's file anyway, without anyone asking for
// it. The settings file is read at startup and never touched again.
//
// Two sets are kept, and the difference between them is the whole point of a preset: GCustom* is what the settings
// file asked for and what the menu edits, GRun* is what is running now. A preset overrides the first without
// overwriting it, so switching back to Custom brings the player's own values back untouched.
//
// GCustom*  what the ini said, and what the menu edits. Vanilla and Recommended never touch these.
// GRun*     what the picture is drawn with right now: the preset's own values, or the custom set under Custom.
